#undef NDEBUG
// Review GY: XES uploads' frame shapes with ints past int64 in their
// timestamp or start columns, and log skeletons keyed by another column.
//
// - An XES column of ints past INT64_MAX (within uint64) used as the
//   timestamp or start key of Heuristics++, the classic performance view,
//   the temporal profile, Alpha or the Inductive miner is typed as pandas
//   types it (uint64 alone, float64 beside floats or gaps, object beside a
//   negative int; Polars' copy UInt64, Float64 or String), so the routes
//   raise pm4py's own errors (or answer) instead of Minera's fallbacks.
// - A log skeleton keyed by another column (log_skeleton_activity_attribute)
//   on the explicit DataFrame and LazyFrame shapes no longer fails the whole
//   mine's presentation: its labels join the process map's activities, as
//   on the default shape.
//
// Expected values are pm4py 2.7.22 black-box on the same inputs
// (review-harness round-gy: tc/mkgy.py, ct/u64.py).
//
// Usage: minera_server_review_gy_tests <minera_server>

